  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reverse Trade Mission - Asia-Pacific Flight Standards, through Koeppen, Elliot &amp; Associates, Ltd.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Asia-Pacific Flight Standards Reverse Trade Mission (RTM) provided an opportunity for delegations from Southeast Asia to travel to the United States to learn about regulatory best practices to improve civil aviation safety and security oversight in their countries. The RTM aimed to help the civil aviation authorities (CAAs) bring flight standards into conformance with International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) guidelines and assist the countries in their pursuit to obtain Category One (Cat I) status under the Federal Aviation Administrations (FAA) International Aviation Safety Assessment Program (IASA). Improving civil aviation safety and security oversight in Southeast Asia and helping the CAAs obtain Cat I status would enable national flag air carriers to provide direct service to the United States.</narrative>
  </description>
